# Upstream pins Dependabot cannot see.
#
# These live HERE, in a plain file, rather than in the workflows that use them —
# and that placement is the whole point. `upstream-pin-bump.yml` opens the PR
# that bumps them using the gw1-mcp-bot App token, and GitHub refuses any App
# push that touches `.github/workflows/**` without `Workflows: write`:
#
#   ! [remote rejected] refusing to allow a GitHub App to create or update
#     workflow `.github/workflows/build-gwtoolbox-plugin.yml`
#     without `workflows` permission
#
# So while the pins sat in workflow YAML the tripwire could detect drift and
# never deliver it: it failed at "Open pull request" on 2026-08-03 and
# 2026-08-10, and the runs before that only looked green because there was no
# drift to report. Granting the App `Workflows: write` would also have worked,
# and was rejected deliberately: it hands an automated identity the right to
# rewrite the CI that reviews everything else, which is the one privilege worth
# withholding from a bot. A data file costs nothing and needs no permission.
#
# Format: KEY=value, one per line, no quotes, no expansion. Consumers load it
# with `grep -E '^[A-Z0-9_]+=' .github/pins.env >> "$GITHUB_ENV"` — the grep is
# what lets these comments exist, since $GITHUB_ENV rejects a line that is not
# an assignment.
#
# Bumping mcp-publisher means changing the VERSION and BOTH digests together.

# The GWToolboxpp commit the AccountExport plugin compiles against. Pinned
# rather than a floating master clone (GW1-04); bump deliberately after reading
# the upstream diff. The plugin build runs on any change to this file, so CI
# proves a bump still compiles.
GWTOOLBOX_COMMIT=ca20ae743551fd24f4fd0653e8a64d5e5b55a820

# Upstream's own pinned vcpkg toolchain commit. Deliberately NOT watched by the
# weekly tripwire: vcpkg master moves dozens of times a day and this is a frozen
# build toolchain, not a feature source. Bump by hand when a dependency needs a
# newer baseline.
VCPKG_COMMIT=ce613c41372b23b1f51333815feb3edd87ef8a8b

# mcp-publisher release + per-arch digests, checked before the binary runs in an
# OIDC job (GW1-05). Digests come from the release assets, which upstream also
# signs with Sigstore.
MCP_PUBLISHER_VERSION=v1.8.0
MCP_PUBLISHER_SHA256_AMD64=1370446bbe74d562608e8005a6ccce02d146a661fbd78674e11cc70b9618d6cf
MCP_PUBLISHER_SHA256_ARM64=c978982c60e1b4903a976de090f04dc4fac4a320daa50704fcad2dbc93433d62
